{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game","id":1494196,"title":"Clans in a Antiquity Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-03T04:09:38-07:00","id":1494196,"title":"Clans in a Antiquity Game","content":"Once more I'm bored and decided to write this up as a means to get ride of some free time. This is for a possible, but unlikely, VtM game in (Late) Antiquity and the Roman Empire. This is a run down of the Clans I would use with some comments on them. As you will notice its a mix between VtM and RfR.<br /> <br /> I hope someone will be somewhat entertained by reading this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Clans</b></span><br /> <br /> <u>A bit more developed Clans</u><br /> <br /> <b>Julii</b> - Roman Clan in the West<br /> <br /> <b>Traditores Clan</b> - Dead and gone by Julii hands<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b> - Created from a nightmarish pact with the Strix rather than a potion made from Tzimisce. See above for metaplot connection<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue</b> - Rather than Roman I intend to run them as Greek and Anatolian with historical branches in Sparta, Syracuse, Makedonia, Epirus etc. And they have sunk their collective fangs deep, very deep, into Constantinople.<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah</b> - A very factionalized Clan. Big City Brujah in Rome and Constantinople and other major cities are close to modern Brujah while those active in Classical Ionian Greek areas or in Phoenicia and North Africa are a bit more in the Dark Ages direction.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador</b> - Ancient basis in Minoan Crete and some ancient Elders were gleefully helpful to aid the Romans in overtaking Greece. Not to many further notes.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavians</b> - Plans to associate them with the Etruscans<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu</b> - Pretty much as in canon<br /> <br /> <b>Vermes</b> - Essentially RfR Nosferatu with a more Requiem than Masquerade angle to this Clan, possibly angling them to be more of albino, hairless and such than twisted like the VtM Nosferatu. They are Roman, although some would say Italic, Clan which has a long history with the city and the Julii. They live mostly as trogdolytes and seem to be digging and driven to look for something, maybe their Ancient, maybe something or someone else entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Mekhet</b> - I always felt weird that only the Setites would be active in Egypt and down the Nile and as such I decided to have two very different Clans coming from this fascinating land<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel</b> - Pretty much standard but given that to my knowledge the &quot;Barbarians&quot; had advanced in most areas through centuries of interaction with the Roman Empire there would be a fair number of Gangrel who are not pissing on trees and barking at wagons.<br /> <br /> <u>Clans I haven't planned much for yet</u><br /> <br /> <b>Daeva</b> - Coming in from Persia but haven't decided on many details yet<br /> <br /> <b>Setites</b> - Pretty much as canon so far<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b> - Not many plans and such yet<br /> <br /> <b>Cappadocians</b> - Kind of like canon with a investment in early Christianity<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri</b> - Not as hunted by the Tremere but still not very common or popular<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce</b> - A serious number in the Balkan provinces. Relation with the Roman Empire varies wildly between Tzimisce broods and even individual Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <b>Assamites</b> - Not many plans here.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b> - Not many plans yet but probably involved with the early Christians<br /> <br /> EDITED: Added part of the Ventrue with Constantinople.<br /> <br /> EDITED II: Split the Nosferatu and Vermes (Nosferatu from RfR) into two Clans<br /> <br /> EDITED III: Added Clan Vermes to the list","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 03-04-2025, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T04:38:00-07:00","id":1494202,"title":"","content":"Assamites would be Greek and Hebrew philosophers, Mithra cultists, and Persian magi.<br /> <br /> Ravnos would mostly be Egyptian merchants, diplomats, sailors, and explorers centered in Alexandria, with smaller factions of gnostics in the Middle East/Levant and hedonists in Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T10:10:20-07:00","id":1494227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494202#post1494202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assamites would be Greek and Hebrew philosophers, Mithra cultists, and Persian magi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, they can fit in nicely within a number of levantine or north african cultures of the period<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494202#post1494202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos would mostly be Egyptian merchants, diplomats, sailors, and explorers centered in Alexandria, with smaller factions of gnostics in the Middle East/Levant and hedonists in Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>OR</b> they could be the Julii - similar weakness, two disciplines out of three and room for something of a twist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T21:55:21-07:00","id":1494282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game#post1494196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tzimisce</b> - Few if any in the Roman Empire</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'd imagine the bulk of the clan would be in Dacia and points East, shouldn't there be quite a few of them in Thrace? Not necessarily the Greek part, but what's now Bulgaria?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T00:07:11-07:00","id":1494289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494227#post1494227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truth be told, they can fit in nicely within a number of levantine or north african cultures of the period<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>OR</b> they could be the Julii - similar weakness, two disciplines out of three and room for something of a twist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Julii as a Ravnos bloodline or could be an interesting twist, especially since it would explain why the Julii don't have an Antediluvian to point at. And I could also see the plotline with shennanigans regarding the Strix and that pact has a certain trickster quality to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494282#post1494282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'd imagine the bulk of the clan would be in Dacia and points East, shouldn't there be quite a few of them in Thrace? Not necessarily the Greek part, but what's now Bulgaria?</div> </div> </div> </div>True that there would reasonably be Tzimisce in the Balkans north of Greece. The first post will be changed to represent this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 10-04-2022, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T00:08:05-07:00","id":1494290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494282#post1494282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'd imagine the bulk of the clan would be in Dacia and points East, shouldn't there be quite a few of them in Thrace? Not necessarily the Greek part, but what's now Bulgaria?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems fair. Thessaly even, with its tales of shapechanging astrologer witch cabals, sounds feasible though part of the hellenic heartland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T00:11:57-07:00","id":1494291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494290#post1494290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Seems fair. Thessaly even, with its tales of shapechanging astrologer witch cabals, sounds feasible though part of the hellenic heartland.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also true and a good idea although I'm afraid I've kind of marked Thessaly in my notes as a stronghold for my &quot;Equites&quot; bloodline which I've posted earlier. Can still be Tzimisce or Gangrel with blood sorcery but probably not in significent numbers or influence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T00:30:21-07:00","id":1494293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494291#post1494291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is also true and a good idea although I'm afraid I've kind of marked Thessaly in my notes as a stronghold for my &quot;Equites&quot; bloodline which I've posted earlier. Can still be Tzimisce or Gangrel with blood sorcery but probably not in significent numbers or influence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say its fine as, though popularized in modern literature in part thanks to the wicca movement, Thessaly IS a region with far more to it in history and mythology than just witchcraft.<br /> <br /> In my own games while once messing with Gargoyles i once hit upon a question &quot;Gangrel, Nosferatu, Tzimisce, don't these 3 clans <i>already</i> have enough shared qualities, territory - and a proclivity for just for unleashing uneducated childer in the wilds - that some <i>unholy hybrid</i> bloodline to spontaneously forming from that might happen even <i>without </i>blood sorcery or some budding cabal's need for troops to jumpstart it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Something that nagged me so much after it dawned on me, i ended up doing so with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leshy\" target=\"_blank\">Leshy</a>, a throng of wandering lords and ladies of the woods, existing in the edges of these clans and blurring the lines that separate them, sometimes grotesque, sometimes not, always connected to the beasts around them, an elusive group of origins shrouded in the past, peculiar <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satyr\" target=\"_blank\">satyr</a>-like beings in a liminar space between caitiff, coven, bloodline and autarkis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-13-2022, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T06:56:10-07:00","id":1494308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494282#post1494282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'd imagine the bulk of the clan would be in Dacia and points East, shouldn't there be quite a few of them in Thrace? Not necessarily the Greek part, but what's now Bulgaria?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably as far south as parts of Macedonia, Greece, and Asia Minor as well, especially the Oburtus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T07:12:29-07:00","id":1494312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494308#post1494308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Probably as far south as parts of Macedonia, Greece, and Asia Minor as well, especially the Oburtus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a possibility although even if Macedonia could be a problem with a significent Tzimisce presence as the northern parts of the Classical Hellenized world in this setting is supposed to be in the sphere of the Ventrue. Effectively where there's a major Hellenic influence south of Thrace and Illyria but north of Thessaly or where Doric Greek was spoken the idea was that you would find the Ventrue in a, most often, dominant position.<br /> <br /> So the question becomes if you think that Tzimisce would be able to either exist there while playing a secondary role to the Ventrue or if they could reasonably coexist there in relative harmony? I mean this from a position of both Clans being associated with rule and power and such.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T08:23:12-07:00","id":1494315,"title":"","content":"Depends. They seemed ok with it in Constantinople.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T09:42:47-07:00","id":1494327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494315#post1494315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends. They seemed ok with it in Constantinople.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but that is from the time of Constantine onwards - the Byzantion that preceded it, according to references in Constantinople by Night, was ruled by neither but Cappadocians instead, with a short Lasombra interegnum under Ektoris after the seeming destruction of most of them beside Alexia Theusa (that later kindred would mistakenly remember as founder).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T13:52:36-07:00","id":1494343,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra being based around Iberia and numerous city states in the Roman Empire and perhaps even Carthage with the Brujah in some form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T21:43:02-07:00","id":1494493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494315#post1494315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends. They seemed ok with it in Constantinople.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I will have to check this up closer and see where it will lead me. Having the Tzimisce and Ventrue, relatively, peacefully share some territory would certainly make for a different setting than the Dark Ages when Ventrue aggression to my knowledge has put them at each other's throats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494327#post1494327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, but that is from the time of Constantine onwards - the Byzantion that preceded it, according to references in Constantinople by Night, was ruled by neither but Cappadocians instead, with a short Lasombra interegnum under Ektoris after the seeming destruction of most of them beside Alexia Theusa (that later kindred would mistakenly remember as founder).</div> </div> </div> </div>Like said, I will investigate this a bit deeper and see what comes from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494343#post1494343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra being based around Iberia and numerous city states in the Roman Empire and perhaps even Carthage with the Brujah in some form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iberia I can see and understand although, if I've understood you correctly, I'm afraid there's somewhat of a rarity regarding city states in the Roman Empire during Late Antiquity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T23:22:53-07:00","id":1494497,"title":"","content":"Constantinople by Night went into a lot of the city/area backstory and history, at least as far as vampires were concerned to as far back as the post-Alexander the Great period, including the 4th generation Toreador ruler Michael and his two lieutenants/lovers, the 4th generation Tzimisce known as The Dracon, and a 4th or 5th generation Ventrue whose name escapes me at the moment. The trio were this weird sort of throuple at least as far back as the end of the Republic IIRC. The Dracon's childer, eventually referred to as the Oburtus (the ghoul family apparently originated from them) apparently tended to be a bit more urban than most, especially among various early monasteries and temples in the region.<br /> <br /> One could, if they wished, just have the Dracons/Oburtus substitute for the Tzimisce as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-07-2022, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T00:20:02-07:00","id":1494503,"title":"","content":"You can check out: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/336923/Vampire-Twentieth-Anniversary-Edition-The-Classical-Age?src=by_author_of_product\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...hor_of_product</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T06:59:52-07:00","id":1494521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494497#post1494497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constantinople by Night went into a lot of the city/area backstory and history, at least as far as vampires were concerned to as far back as the post-Alexander the Great period, including the 4th generation Toreador ruler Michael and his two lieutenants/lovers, the 4th generation Tzimisce known as The Dracon, and a 4th or 5th generation Ventrue whose name escapes me at the moment. The trio were this weird sort of throuple at least as far back as the end of the Republic IIRC. The Dracon's childer, eventually referred to as the Oburtus (the ghoul family apparently originated from them) apparently tended to be a bit more urban than most, especially among various early monasteries and temples in the region.<br /> <br /> One could, if they wished, just have the Dracons/Oburtus substitute for the Tzimisce as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds interesting. I'll add it to my list of sources and see what more goodies there are in that supplement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494503#post1494503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can check out: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/336923/Vampire-Twentieth-Anniversary-Edition-The-Classical-Age?src=by_author_of_product\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...hor_of_product</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm a afraid I already have that and almost all the companion supplements but its really useful for this project so its welcome that its also mentioned here a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T09:29:11-07:00","id":1494528,"title":"","content":"[<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Iberia I can see and understand although, if I've understood you correctly, I'm afraid there's somewhat of a rarity regarding city states in the Roman Empire during Late Antiquity.<br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> Yes I felt that Iberia would be a great place for the most of the major players of the Lasombra clan, but then I thought that they have a fondness for the sea and felt that they would have a presence in any Roman cities that were major port communities like Venice and I thought Carthage would be a good place for them as it was a major power in the old world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T11:26:57-07:00","id":1494538,"title":"","content":"Sicily is probably a stronghold of the Roman Lasombra, along with Corsica and Sardinia, the Balearic Islands, Massilia and Narbonensis, and other nearby regions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T04:21:29-07:00","id":1494666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494528#post1494528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<br /> Yes I felt that Iberia would be a great place for the most of the major players of the Lasombra clan, but then I thought that they have a fondness for the sea and felt that they would have a presence in any Roman cities that were major port communities like Venice and I thought Carthage would be a good place for them as it was a major power in the old world.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494538#post1494538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sicily is probably a stronghold of the Roman Lasombra, along with Corsica and Sardinia, the Balearic Islands, Massilia and Narbonensis, and other nearby regions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its true that it would make sense for the Lasombra to be a power in the Western Mediterranean on the islands and along the coast, as well as through Iberia.<br /> <br /> In regards to Carthage it would make for a potential interesting plotlinke or hook that the Lasombra have shepherded the Roman Carthage into importance after the Carthage that harbored Brujah and Baali* was destroyed. Both in regards to a different city in the west, a potential conflict between aspects of the Brujah and Lasombra Clans as well as remains from the Old Carthage surfacing without anyone per necessity being around who knows for certain what what it is or what to do about it.<br /> <br /> *I'm pretty sure that I will need to re-write some stuff here as I personally dislike the Baali to the point of removing them from the setting.<br /> <br /> EDITED: Fixed some stuff with quotations and such.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T11:26:48-07:00","id":1494685,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t care for them either and that\u2019s why I went with the Lasombra clan as being involved in Carthage with the Brujah and Assamites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T12:54:44-07:00","id":1494693,"title":"","content":"The idea of including the Lasombra (or at least a faction of them) in with the Carthage stuff goes make sense with their thematic associations with being anti-Ventrue, tied to the Sea (the Punic War decided control over the western Mediterranean), and their later association with the Basil (such as with that \u2018Dark Angel\u2019 bloodline of theirs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T15:59:47-07:00","id":1494702,"title":"","content":"Carthage always seemed like an odd hill for the Brujah to decide to die on. I realize that it's a result of it being 1992, the two Sabbat clans being nothing more than a pair of &quot;blink and you'll miss them&quot; names buried in the text, and someone deciding that the Punic Wars sounds like an explanation for why the punk rebel idealist Brujah have always hated the conformist corporate suit Ventrue, but hindsight only makes it weirder. <br /> <br /> As you both say, given how the Lasombra were given ties to the sea, especially the ancient Mediterranean, were so strongly associated with Iberia, Sicily, and Northern Africa (all Carthaginian territories), and the Carthaginians coming from the ancient sea-fairing Phoenicians, they make a much more logical choice of the clan most associated with Carthage. Thus the Punic Wars then become a logical explanation for the long running rivalry between the Lasombra and Ventrue, with various Lasombra holding grudges which carry on through the Roman Empire and into the Dark Ages and beyond. (At that point, you probably have a bunch of things like rivalry between Iberian and German branches of the Hapsburg dynasty/empires, Spanish Catholics verses German and English Protestants, and so forth just adding to it.) <br /> <br /> In contrast, given their ancient reputation as intellectuals and philosophers, the fact that two of the big name clan members in Chicago by Night were from Ancient Greece, and how much the Brujah section in Dark Ages's Keepers of the Word focuses on Ancient Greece, one would expect them to be primarily connected to that ancient culture and territory. In that case, the Roman conquest of Greece become a possible bone of contention between members of the two clans. Such a thing could also be compounded by Rome's mythical connections to ancient Troy via the Aeneid, perhaps with certain Roman elders having ties that lost Bronze Age (Hittite?) city state/kingdom, and still holding grudges about it. (This ironically flips the traditional narrative on its head, with the Ventrue being the ones bitterly pining for a lost cause.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T21:06:21-07:00","id":1494710,"title":"","content":"I don't have the book handy to look up specifics, but I recall the revised Giovanni clanbook's history section discussing parts of the mortal family's history back in Roman times. I can't remember when the Cappadocians started embracing members, but it offers an interesting plot hook for the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T10:15:23-07:00","id":1494794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494710#post1494710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the book handy to look up specifics, but I recall the revised Giovanni clanbook's history section discussing parts of the mortal family's history back in Roman times. I can't remember when the Cappadocians started embracing members, but it offers an interesting plot hook for the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The accepted version is that the Giovanni were embraced early in the 11th century. But they admit that there might be members of there family who might be members of other clans like Ventrue or even Lasombra.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T23:04:54-07:00","id":1494909,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they'd been a rich and powerful mercantile family with an interest in the occult for at least a millennium before Cappadocious decided to recruit them into his clan. It stands to reason that there would have been individuals embraced into the other clans and bloodlines active in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T14:36:53-07:00","id":1494938,"title":"","content":"Now for some reason I'm attracted that having a faction of the Tzismce being in Macendonia and shaping some the tribes &amp; kingdoms in that region and having a rivalry with the others clans active in Greece.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T03:21:30-07:00","id":1495104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494685#post1494685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn\u2019t care for them either and that\u2019s why I went with the Lasombra clan as being involved in Carthage with the Brujah and Assamites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cheers! To be honest I didn't think for myself that the Lasombra would replace the Baali in the first Carthage but rather that they would move in with the new Roman Carthage after the original Punic one had been destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494693#post1494693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of including the Lasombra (or at least a faction of them) in with the Carthage stuff goes make sense with their thematic associations with being anti-Ventrue, tied to the Sea (the Punic War decided control over the western Mediterranean), and their later association with the Basil (such as with that \u2018Dark Angel\u2019 bloodline of theirs).</div> </div> </div> </div>True that. See above for my own thoughts on this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494702#post1494702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carthage always seemed like an odd hill for the Brujah to decide to die on. I realize that it's a result of it being 1992, the two Sabbat clans being nothing more than a pair of &quot;blink and you'll miss them&quot; names buried in the text, and someone deciding that the Punic Wars sounds like an explanation for why the punk rebel idealist Brujah have always hated the conformist corporate suit Ventrue, but hindsight only makes it weirder.<br /> <br /> As you both say, given how the Lasombra were given ties to the sea, especially the ancient Mediterranean, were so strongly associated with Iberia, Sicily, and Northern Africa (all Carthaginian territories), and the Carthaginians coming from the ancient sea-fairing Phoenicians, they make a much more logical choice of the clan most associated with Carthage. Thus the Punic Wars then become a logical explanation for the long running rivalry between the Lasombra and Ventrue, with various Lasombra holding grudges which carry on through the Roman Empire and into the Dark Ages and beyond. (At that point, you probably have a bunch of things like rivalry between Iberian and German branches of the Hapsburg dynasty/empires, Spanish Catholics verses German and English Protestants, and so forth just adding to it.)<br /> <br /> In contrast, given their ancient reputation as intellectuals and philosophers, the fact that two of the big name clan members in Chicago by Night were from Ancient Greece, and how much the Brujah section in Dark Ages's Keepers of the Word focuses on Ancient Greece, one would expect them to be primarily connected to that ancient culture and territory. In that case, the Roman conquest of Greece become a possible bone of contention between members of the two clans. Such a thing could also be compounded by Rome's mythical connections to ancient Troy via the Aeneid, perhaps with certain Roman elders having ties that lost Bronze Age (Hittite?) city state/kingdom, and still holding grudges about it. (This ironically flips the traditional narrative on its head, with the Ventrue being the ones bitterly pining for a lost cause.)</div> </div> </div> </div>All good ideas about the subject of the Brujah-vs-Ventrue feud.<br /> <br /> For myself I imagine that [Brujah] is the reason alot of Brujah went down with Carthage. I ( think that I) know that Ilyres was in Carthage and thus that would have pulled alot of Brujah with it and create a center for the Clan in the city. And that in particular the &quot;loyalist&quot; faction of Brujah in relation to their Ancient would have kept themselves in Carthage and then fought tooth-and-nail against the attackers.<br /> <br /> But in regards to Greece I agree with you and funnily enought I also intended to associate the Ventrue heavily with Anatolia and the Hittites in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494710#post1494710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the book handy to look up specifics, but I recall the revised Giovanni clanbook's history section discussing parts of the mortal family's history back in Roman times. I can't remember when the Cappadocians started embracing members, but it offers an interesting plot hook for the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>if the Giovanni goes back into Antiquity then that would also help me in bringing the Clan into the ancient nights given how I think that they actually do the Necromancer Clan thing better than the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494909#post1494909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they'd been a rich and powerful mercantile family with an interest in the occult for at least a millennium before Cappadocious decided to recruit them into his clan. It stands to reason that there would have been individuals embraced into the other clans and bloodlines active in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that they operate in northern Italy, am I the only one who thinks of family members Embraced into Clan Tremere before the Cappadocians made their definitive move? Now a Cainite with loyalties to both the Family and to the Pyramid is a conflict of interests that one could do something with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1494938#post1494938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for some reason I'm attracted that having a faction of the Tzismce being in Macendonia and shaping some the tribes &amp; kingdoms in that region and having a rivalry with the others clans active in Greece.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be cool. Although I'm afraid that in my own take on it Macedonia is a historical Ventrue stronghold. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T10:53:28-07:00","id":1495128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1495104#post1495104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cheers! To be honest I didn't think for myself that the Lasombra would replace the Baali in the first Carthage but rather that they would move in with the new Roman Carthage after the original Punic one had been destroyed.<br /> <br /> Both ideas can work equally well if it's done properly Gurkhal. In fact I'm even entertaining the idea of not having Brujah involved in Carthage and being focused more in Athens and there sphere of influence. I know that I'm taking a big liberty with the lore there in regards to the setting. But there are others on the board who have said that they do take liberties like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That could be cool. Although I'm afraid that in my own take on it Macedonia is a historical Ventrue stronghold. :</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I could totally see that happening and even a Ventrue ancient taking an interest in the family that would produce Phillp The 2nd and his son Alexander The Great or even being an ancenstor of that family. I toyed with that idea in Vampire The Requiem with a Mekhet being there remote founder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T11:09:27-07:00","id":1495129,"title":"","content":"The Daeva I could see as a widespread clan that has it's fingers in every major kingdom in the ancient world that has considerable size and influence with all sorts of cults of all types. So they could be merchants, storytellers, slave traders, priests and the ever popular cruel nobles that could make Caguila take a step back in horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-17-2022, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T11:57:02-07:00","id":1495365,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Setites, there was, apparently, an ancient Italian goddess named Angitia, associated with snakes, snake-charmers, and witches, as well as healing. Her worship was centered among the Marsian peoples in the Central Apennine mountain region (central Italy), and the 2nd century BC Roman historian Gnaeus Gellius describes her as being the granddaughter of Helios and the sister of Circe and Medea. However, because she was so heavily associated with healing, her cult might also make an interesting angle for Roman Salubri. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in Iberia, you have the Basque god Sugaar, a storm/thunder deity usually pictured as a dragon or serpent. Unfortunately, there doesn't seem to be a lot of surviving information about him.<br /> <br /> And in Greece, you have a number of possibilities. One is the story of Ophion/Ophioneus (&quot;serpent&quot;), who ruled the world before Chronos came to power. This is the sort of thing that can play into the Setites' belief that they've been unjustly supplanted by other (Aeonic) gods. Likewise that of Python, the original goddess of Delphi, who was slain and supplanted by the sun god Apollo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T09:00:09-07:00","id":1495830,"title":"","content":"Now with the Mekhet it's a no brainer that they would have the strongest ties to Egypt &amp; Greece as Vizers, Priests, Scholars, Spymasters and Cult Leaders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T13:04:20-07:00","id":1496123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1495365#post1495365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Setites, there was, apparently, an ancient Italian goddess named Angitia, associated with snakes, snake-charmers, and witches, as well as healing. Her worship was centered among the Marsian peoples in the Central Apennine mountain region (central Italy), and the 2nd century BC Roman historian Gnaeus Gellius describes her as being the granddaughter of Helios and the sister of Circe and Medea. However, because she was so heavily associated with healing, her cult might also make an interesting angle for Roman Salubri.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in Iberia, you have the Basque god Sugaar, a storm/thunder deity usually pictured as a dragon or serpent. Unfortunately, there doesn't seem to be a lot of surviving information about him.<br /> <br /> And in Greece, you have a number of possibilities. One is the story of Ophion/Ophioneus (&quot;serpent&quot;), who ruled the world before Chronos came to power. This is the sort of thing that can play into the Setites' belief that they've been unjustly supplanted by other (Aeonic) gods. Likewise that of Python, the original goddess of Delphi, who was slain and supplanted by the sun god Apollo.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is certainly an nice rundown for a person like me \u2013 informative and interesting to read. Other than the school and university education, most of what I know in regard to gods / deities, and also various beliefs, faiths, and religious organizations comes from relatively small amount of independant fact checking and research, and also from computer games like Shogun: Total War 2, Medieval Total War 2, Civilization 4, Civilization 5, Age of Mythology, Heroes of Might and Magic 4 and also Europa Universalis 3. Another source is of course role-playing games like WoD, Song of Ice and Fire (GoT) RPG, Pathfinder, and of course Dungeons and Dragons RPG.<br /> <br /> Could you please recommend / point to sources (wether books or articles) with interesting and reliable analysis and facts in regard to deities / gods, and possibly also religious outlooks, in regard to dragons and healing (and related concepts and ideas, if appropriate). You would have my thanks for this, as I am very interested in regard these topics and also of course in regard to related areas of knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-03T06:32:26-07:00","id":1496163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1495129#post1495129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva I could see as a widespread clan that has it's fingers in every major kingdom in the ancient world that has considerable size and influence with all sorts of cults of all types. So they could be merchants, storytellers, slave traders, priests and the ever popular cruel nobles that could make Caguila take a step back in horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. I haven't thought to much about the Daeva so far but I figure more stuff will come to mind when I get around to research ancient Iran and such. Although I figure that the first task should be to differentiate them from the Clans that are roughly angling towards the same kind of style. Primarily the Toreador and the Setites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1495365#post1495365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Setites, there was, apparently, an ancient Italian goddess named Angitia, associated with snakes, snake-charmers, and witches, as well as healing. Her worship was centered among the Marsian peoples in the Central Apennine mountain region (central Italy), and the 2nd century BC Roman historian Gnaeus Gellius describes her as being the granddaughter of Helios and the sister of Circe and Medea. However, because she was so heavily associated with healing, her cult might also make an interesting angle for Roman Salubri.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in Iberia, you have the Basque god Sugaar, a storm/thunder deity usually pictured as a dragon or serpent. Unfortunately, there doesn't seem to be a lot of surviving information about him.<br /> <br /> And in Greece, you have a number of possibilities. One is the story of Ophion/Ophioneus (&quot;serpent&quot;), who ruled the world before Chronos came to power. This is the sort of thing that can play into the Setites' belief that they've been unjustly supplanted by other (Aeonic) gods. Likewise that of Python, the original goddess of Delphi, who was slain and supplanted by the sun god Apollo.</div> </div> </div> </div>The positive view of serpents in the ancient polytheistic world is of course known, at least in the Greco-Roman world, and I don't find it odd at all that there would be healing goddesses connected with snakes.<br /> <br /> But like you say, and those are all solid ideas in regards to snakes in Greek mythology, there's plenty of material to angle in the Setites towards. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1495830#post1495830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now with the Mekhet it's a no brainer that they would have the strongest ties to Egypt &amp; Greece as Vizers, Priests, Scholars, Spymasters and Cult Leaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the Mekhet I agree with the Egyptian connection but I'm a little questioning about the Greek one. Care to elaborate on why the Mekhet would have a connection there?<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> To move this forward a bit.<br /> <br /> In regards to Clan Daeva I figure that I should change their Discipline set from the Brujah set one to the following: Presence, Fortitude and Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Presence is a must-have for the Clan's concept and I figure that the idea of &quot;whisperer/tempter in the dark&quot; like vices would work with them better than insight or control over animals.<br /> <br /> And since I wanted to separate them from, perhaps most importantly, the Toreador, I went with Fortitude for their physical Discipline together with a theme of them, like vices, hard to destroy or resist. The resist part also played a part in giving them Presence.<br /> <br /> I might make changes as I research more or from further feedback but that's how it stands right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T11:56:12-07:00","id":1496210,"title":"","content":"I figured that the Mekhet with there love for lore of all sorts would travel all over the ancient world and I thought Greece would be a major port for them esspecially when you had folks like Alexander The Great taking over and setting up a lineage that would include Cleoprata and that they would have there interest sparked from that encounter.<br /> <br /> Also I choose the two locations as I have a fondness for ancient Egypt &amp; Greece and went with that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-04-2022, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T12:06:16-07:00","id":1496213,"title":"","content":"<br /> *****<br /> <br /> To move this forward a bit.<br /> <br /> In regards to Clan Daeva I figure that I should change their Discipline set from the Brujah set one to the following: Presence, Fortitude and Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Presence is a must-have for the Clan's concept and I figure that the idea of &quot;whisperer/tempter in the dark&quot; like vices would work with them better than insight or control over animals.<br /> <br /> And since I wanted to separate them from, perhaps most importantly, the Toreador, I went with Fortitude for their physical Discipline together with a theme of them, like vices, hard to destroy or resist. The resist part also played a part in giving them Presence.<br /> <br /> I might make changes as I research more or from further feedback but that's how it stands right now.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I see no issue with the changed discipline spread at all and considering how in the first edition they had a hard time resisiting there vices and getting into trouble with that problem. I'd would want to be able to withstand inhuman amounts of punishment and be able to disappear when needed. You know come to think of it they could be a better alternative then the Baali if you want to go that route. A clan of hedonistic monsters that cause nothing but trouble and endanger the masquerade and that the other clans will put aside there issues and stamp them down.<br /> <br /> On a different note do you have any plans of having the Tremere or The Malkavians having ties to the Oracole Of Delphie? Both groups certainly wouldn't be to out of place there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-04-2022, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T21:41:12-07:00","id":1496285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1496210#post1496210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured that the Mekhet with there love for lore of all sorts would travel all over the ancient world and I thought Greece would be a major port for them esspecially when you had folks like Alexander The Great taking over and setting up a lineage that would include Cleoprata and that they would have there interest sparked from that encounter.<br /> <br /> Also I choose the two locations as I have a fondness for ancient Egypt &amp; Greece and went with that reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>True about the Mekhet and lore, so I can see that angle. Even while I myself would not, in order to not crowd Greece to much, have Greece stand out but just be another area where Mekhet seem to gather.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1496213#post1496213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*****<br /> <br /> To move this forward a bit.<br /> <br /> In regards to Clan Daeva I figure that I should change their Discipline set from the Brujah set one to the following: Presence, Fortitude and Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Presence is a must-have for the Clan's concept and I figure that the idea of &quot;whisperer/tempter in the dark&quot; like vices would work with them better than insight or control over animals.<br /> <br /> And since I wanted to separate them from, perhaps most importantly, the Toreador, I went with Fortitude for their physical Discipline together with a theme of them, like vices, hard to destroy or resist. The resist part also played a part in giving them Presence.<br /> <br /> I might make changes as I research more or from further feedback but that's how it stands right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no issue with the changed discipline spread at all and considering how in the first edition they had a hard time resisiting there vices and getting into trouble with that problem. I'd would want to be able to withstand inhuman amounts of punishment and be able to disappear when needed. You know come to think of it they could be a better alternative then the Baali if you want to go that route. A clan of hedonistic monsters that cause nothing but trouble and endanger the masquerade and that the other clans will put aside there issues and stamp them down.<br /> <br /> On a different note do you have any plans of having the Tremere or The Malkavians having ties to the Oracole Of Delphie? Both groups certainly wouldn't be to out of place there.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> I will probably not try to move them into the Baali niche, that will be left empty, but the Daeva as both vice-inducing and themselves vice-ridden could probably work pretty well. I may need to check over the Ravnos to ensure they don't end up to close to each other in the weakness department but other than that it looks like a good angle on them.<br /> <br /> EDITED: As for the oracle of Delphi I would think that the Malkavians and Mekhet have more interest in it than the Tremere. As I think I wrote in the first post I'm tying the Tremere with the Strix so they are more focused in the west than the east. At least at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T13:21:55-08:00","id":1496530,"title":"","content":"Fair enough Gurkhal in regards to Greece and not wanting to overpopulate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T13:26:37-08:00","id":1496533,"title":"","content":"I do like your idea of the Cappadocians &amp; the Tremere wanting to woo the Giovanni family in that time period and seeing what clan they would decide to join. It certainly would turn the lore on it's head.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T16:14:04-08:00","id":1496555,"title":"","content":"How about Animalism for Daeva? So they have Presence, but they can also manipulate baser parts of the psyche. Maybe they have owl familiars, to make use of more of the animal part of that discipline and play up their relationship with Lillith (possibly rewritten to refer to Noddist Lillith). And then they could have Dur-An-Ki, to serve as intermediaries with the gods (by doing drugs with kine) and further ensorcell respectable Roman kindred. Although Dur-An-Ki or another type blood sorcery, could be a good swap for Mekhet, to represent part of the thousands of years of arcane lore that they keep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T23:23:07-08:00","id":1496576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1496533#post1496533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like your idea of the Cappadocians &amp; the Tremere wanting to woo the Giovanni family in that time period and seeing what clan they would decide to join. It certainly would turn the lore on it's head.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you liked it. Of course the Clan that gets the Giovanni will embrace (pun intended) a figurative snake. But there should be some interesting potential plot developments from how that goes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1496555#post1496555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Animalism for Daeva? So they have Presence, but they can also manipulate baser parts of the psyche. Maybe they have owl familiars, to make use of more of the animal part of that discipline and play up their relationship with Lillith (possibly rewritten to refer to Noddist Lillith). And then they could have Dur-An-Ki, to serve as intermediaries with the gods (by doing drugs with kine) and further ensorcell respectable Roman kindred. Although Dur-An-Ki or another type blood sorcery, could be a good swap for Mekhet, to represent part of the thousands of years of arcane lore that they keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool ideas. I think that for the main clan I've mostly made up my mind about the Discipline spread, although the opening for a bloodline or &quot;clan version&quot; with Animalism and a owl and Lilith connection/theme is there. I will admit that I like some parts of the Requiem approach to bloodlines in that they can be used to represent takes on a clan's theme that is a bit more narrow than the whole clan but broader than an individual member of said clan.<br /> <br /> As for the blood sorcery I'm not very well versed at this point. But to have both Assamite and Daeva share the Dur-An-Ki would make sense to me and I might let the Mekhet in on Setite Sorcery which to my knowledge is heavily Egyptian in theme and so would fit well with the Mekhet and their connection to Egypt.<br /> <br /> But just like the Tremere are magical kleptocrats so the Mekhet could be for arcane and mystical power and knowledge. Might be also be a point of contention, and possible stories, as both clans would be out to hoard and &quot;aquire&quot; magical power and knowledge from other sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T07:29:57-08:00","id":1496592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1496123#post1496123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please recommend / point to sources (wether books or articles) with interesting and reliable analysis and facts in regard to deities / gods, and possibly also religious outlooks, in regard to dragons and healing (and related concepts and ideas, if appropriate). You would have my thanks for this, as I am very interested in regard these topics and also of course in regard to related areas of knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really an expert. It's mostly a lifetime of reading, including where I used to frequently pick up various mythology encyclopedias when they were in the discount sections at the various big box bookstore chains. <br /> <br /> As far as online sources, <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/greek-mythology/dragons.html\" target=\"_blank\">theoi.com</a> is a fairly deep collection of Greek Mythology. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T11:47:02-08:00","id":1497742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1496592#post1496592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really an expert. It's mostly a lifetime of reading, including where I used to frequently pick up various mythology encyclopedias when they were in the discount sections at the various big box bookstore chains.<br /> <br /> As far as online sources, <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/greek-mythology/dragons.html\" target=\"_blank\">theoi.com</a> is a fairly deep collection of Greek Mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for linking this website, it might certainly come in useful. Maybe especially in regard to me making definite progress in regard to designing personal computer games (whether standalone games or mods, this remains to be seen), which I have been looking forward to do since at least some time. This site seems certainly more varied and comprehensive than sources which I have encountered and read before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T08:52:17-08:00","id":1498078,"title":"","content":"You know I have a soft spot for the Nagaraja bloodline and wonder how they would be handled in this setting. I guess they could have a subtle presence in Constainople and have loose ties to the Cappadocians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T20:53:18-08:00","id":1498182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1498078#post1498078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I have a soft spot for the Nagaraja bloodline and wonder how they would be handled in this setting. I guess they could have a subtle presence in Constainople and have loose ties to the Cappadocians.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far I have no ideas about what to do with the Nagaraja as I know far to little about them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T21:25:21-08:00","id":1498184,"title":"","content":"They originate in Bronze Age India from a group of Thanatoic necromancers who turned themselves into vampires. Except that their weakness required them to consume the flesh of their victims along with their blood. (They are effectively a walking blasphemy to nearly every faith in the subcontinent, including certain vampire ones, so they never had many members, even after joining the eastern part of the Black Hand cult.) Most tended to focus on their necromancy experiments.<br /> Various Indian states, especially the Greeco-Indian successor ones in the northwest, did trade with Rome, including Indian merchants and travelers ending up in Rome and other major cities. It's not impossible for a few Nagaraja to end up in Rome, Constantinople, or Alexandria, possibility trying to pass themselves off as Cappadocians and studying Western arts involving the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T11:55:39-08:00","id":1498556,"title":"","content":"I find them interesting for the creepy factor and like to see them get more &quot;screen time&quot; so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T21:39:13-08:00","id":1500575,"title":"","content":"EDITED: I'll chew a bit on the Nagaraja and see what may come out. The idea of cannibal necromancers is cool, although given the presence of both Clan Cappadocian along with the recruitment, or at least courting, of the Giovanni family's ancient ancestors might lead to the necromancer scene get crowded if not handled well.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> One idea I've had about this setting is that the Toreador can perhaps have their brand of horrific in casual and, rather wasteful, gathering and spending of slaves, servants and lovers? The idea here is that Toreador tend, not everyone but its a common practice, to gather and enslave through emotonal manipulation both human, Kindred and supernatural servants around them and which are used up and discarded without a second thought. Leading the Toreador to be different from others whom rely to a large degree on influence and power over mortals and such for their strength, like Ventrue, Julii and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> I particular like the idea of the Toreador gathering mythological creatues to themselves, like Bull-Men, Satyrs etc. who loves, lives and dies for charming, beautiful, sophisticated and ultimately uncaring masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 01-18-2023, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T10:53:09-08:00","id":1500745,"title":"","content":"That sounds very much how I personally view the Toreador clan in general and injected that into my Brujah character whenever he is asked on his feelings about the other clans in geneeral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T22:28:12-08:00","id":1500812,"title":"","content":"Ok, so a post about the Clan which I feel that I've fleshed out the most at this point in time. Namely Clan Brujah. Even though its fleshed out quite a bit I've tried to trim down on the word count as to not write an essay and get to the point.<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah in the Ancient Nights</b><br /> <br /> The Brujah in the Roman nights have spread across the empire with historical strongholds in Punic North Africa, Phoenicia, Ionia and Attica. Since time immemorial the Clans has been an urban one and tied to cities which has also left large numbers of younger Brujah in Rome, Constantinople, Antioch and Alexandria. Thus the cultural division within the Clan are roughly between those Brujah of a more traditional bent in or connected with the historical bastions and those in the big cities of the empire.<br /> <br /> Generally the traditionalist Brujah in the old lands adhere to a philosphical interests while those in the big cities are more aligned with political and religious engagements or just live the big city life in a hard, fast and dangerous way. Thus the way I see it is that the Brujah of the big cities are more like the modern Brujah while those in the old lands are more in the Dark Ages form. <br /> <br /> <b>[Brujah]</b><br /> <br /> I've decided to skip a little on the Ilyres and Troile storyline and instead run [Brujah] as a creature which used Soul Mastery, seen below, of unprecedented skill to wander both across the world and between bodies for millennia before finally disappearing from records for a final time with the fall of Carthage. A big inspiration, I will admit, for this version of [Brujah] has been the &quot;Voices of Nerat&quot; as found in the &quot;Tyranny&quot; computer game (I love that game even if I haven't finished it, yet).<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodlines, Versions and Factions</b>, and I most strongly apologize for butchering non-English names here, please forgive me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Also note that the most factions are not necessarily intended to be Brujah-only, but factions which I can see are very attractive to the Brujah, if one goes by stereotype.<br /> <br /> <i>Aresidae</i> - A curious but dangerous throwback to older times, this bloodline has but two Disciplines, Potence and Celerity and must roll constant hunger frenzies against the presence of other Brujah which they seem to recognize by some undefined ability, along with a compulsion to Embrace mortals from time to time. Its believed that these presents some kind of early version of the Clan or a discarded tool created by [Brujah] for some purpose with many speculations about what that purpose might have been.<br /> <br /> <i>Molochim</i> - Replaced Presence with Dominate. Originally created by [Brujah] to serve its needs in Carthage, the fall of the Ancient has since then released this bloodline to forge their own way although cults of the Ancient are common among their ranks. Many old and conservative Molochim maintain a loyalty and nostalgia expressed through ancestor cults to [Brujah]. The old devoutions, as detailed a bit below, are primarily found and taught among the cultists of the Ancestor Cult of [Brujah]<br /> <br /> <i>True Brujah</i> - Replace Temporis with Auspex. My policy of cutting down on unique Disicplines is at work here and I feel that Auspex can work just as well for the themes of the True Brujah bloodline.<br /> <br /> <i>Cult of [Brujah]</i> - Gives access to learn &quot;Soul Mastery&quot; Devoutions. I really like the system of bonuses in mechanics for buying certain stuff so that's something I intend to adapt from VtR. Its essentially a cult devoted to [Brujah] and its practices, with some different factions within it from seeing [Brujah] as a philosphical teacher/mentor/example or recognized ancestor to outright seeking a ressurection of the Ancient or holding to a prophecy that [Brujah] will one day return to rule its Clan in the flesh.<br /> <br /> <i>Neo-Gracchi</i> - Buy Allies, Contacts and Rhetorical (essentially a porting over from Requiem for Rome) Merits connected with an urban setting for half the price in XP. Very similar to the modern Brujah in wanting to affect change for the poor and lower classes by both direct actions as well as political manovering in Elysium.<br /> <br /> Other factions I've considered are <i>Perikleans</i> (Democratic orators and warriors connected with the Grecophone world), <i>Caesarians</i> (thinks that changes in society can only be achived after control over society has been won by armed force and generally connected with the big cities), <i>Hoplites</i> (Decentralists, local rule and generally connected with the Grecophone world). <br /> <br /> <b>Soul Mastery Devoutions</b> - This is kind of a work in progress but the the powers I've so far decided on are the following, and I hope to add more in the future.<br /> <br /> <i>Group Diablerie</i> - Spend a WP dot to participate in a collective diablerie. Each participant that spends a dot gains part of the benefits for a solo diablerie in addition to the dark aura of a diablerie<br /> <br /> <i>Soul Shackles</i> - Instead of eating a soul the character takes the soul into its own body as a prisoner to be communicated with, later diableriezed or something else entirely<br /> <br /> <i>Blossom of Hunger</i> - Induced a diablerist hunger frenzy in a targeted Kindred<br /> <br /> <i>Merging Souls</i> - Merge souls within yourself with each other, the more successes one gets on the role the most control over the merging process the user has<br /> <br /> <i>Transfer Soul</i> - Bring a soul held within one's self into a new body that one is drinking from. if there's a soul within a body that leads to a battle between the two souls. Taking a Kindred's soul into a living body transform that body into a Kindred body. Only works with mundane human, ghoul or Kindred bodies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T08:00:54-08:00","id":1500838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1500812#post1500812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> Also note that the most factions are not necessarily intended to be Brujah-only, but factions which I can see are very attractive to the Brujah, if one goes by stereotype.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which other Kindred / Vampire Clans could be involved with these factions \\ groups \\ organizations ? Would possible or guaranteed benefits and also as well level / degree of participation be equal, or at the very least comparable, between Brujah and non-Brujah Kindred belonging to these groups ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T10:55:07-08:00","id":1500852,"title":"","content":"I could see the Ventrue and maybe the Tzismce being interested in the Molocim as it would appeal to there love of traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-21-2023, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T06:21:34-08:00","id":1501028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1500838#post1500838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which other Kindred / Vampire Clans could be involved with these factions \\ groups \\ organizations ? Would possible or guaranteed benefits and also as well level / degree of participation be equal, or at the very least comparable, between Brujah and non-Brujah Kindred belonging to these groups ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Well, I figure that most of the factions could find some attraction with other Clans and bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Cult of [Brujah] - A variety of Kindred whom for one reason or another finds more personal connection between themselves and one or another image of [Brujah] as well as those seeking the esoteric arts of &quot;Soul Mastery&quot;. So Ventrue, Tzimisce, Toreador, Gangrel and so on.<br /> <br /> Neo-Grachii: I will agree that most likely this i perhaps the one that's going to find itself with a Brujah membership but urban Kindred wanting to change the status que for their benefit could also make their way here.<br /> <br /> Perikleans - Gangrel and Nosferatu might be somewhat attracted by the democratic notions expressed.<br /> <br /> Caesarians - Here I would think that even young Kindred from Julii, Ventrue, Lasombra etc. could be found as they would want to affect change and rise higher in the style of Caesar and Augustus which might be more palatable to more of their members than say the Periklean way of democratic empowerment.<br /> <br /> Hoplites - In particular I think that Gangrel and old Greek Ventrue and Toreador would like this way of local-rule as they would want to run their domains without outsider meddling as much as possible, and in various ways stall, hinder or slow down dictates from some central authority imposed on them. Any Tzimisce who holds lands in Grecophone lands might be tripping over itself to run things this way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1500852#post1500852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see the Ventrue and maybe the Tzismce being interested in the Molocim as it would appeal to there love of traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know about the Molochim as its supposed to be a Brujah bloodline but I can see Ventrue anda Tzimisce interest in the Cult of [Brujah] for the reasons you've mentioned above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:23:32-08:00","id":1501497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1501028#post1501028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Well, I figure that most of the factions could find some attraction with other Clans and bloodlines.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is certainly a nice expansion of the original description. Thank you for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:21:56-07:00","id":1514839,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Time to get some life into this thread again. This time it\u2019s a kind of low-hanging fruit in the form of Clan Julii that's getting a post about it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Julii in Ancient Nights</b><br /> <br /> Few Clans carries such strong associations as the Julii to a specific group of kine. Roman, republican and pagan the Clan of Julii holds the Eternal City and most of Italia in a vice-like grip. Unlike most other Clans the Julii have no long and extensive history outside of the history of mortal Roman state. Even their own Ancient is strangely absent from the myths and legends that so surround the other Ancients of the Clans. This leads to unflattering rumours regarding origin ranging from the accursed Striges to being a mere bloodline of another, proper, Clan and often in that case a Clan of ill repute in Roman eyes.<br /> <br /> As could be expected Clan Julii hails almost entirely from Italian stock and with a larger number of lineages drawing their origins from distinguished Italian gens. Kindred and human lineage are often heavily intervened with each other's fate and actions. This has lead to a great sense of purpose and prestige but at the cost of decline as the world is moving away from Rome itself and Italia is becoming but another province in the empire while the Julii willingly declines the possibility of a greater talent pool from outside of their mortal lineages. Even in decline the Julii control huge resources and there is yet time for the famous Roman pragmatism to alter the development, or so many young Julii hope.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Julii not Embraced according to the familial principles of keeping the bloodline within one\u2019s proper gens are seen as bastard children, or worse, and kept as second-rate members of the Clan, and in some cases denied to actually be Julii at all. Dark rumours speak of Julii Elders bringing destruction to Julii bearing their vitae but not of their gens.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Very much an urban Clan the Julii is almost only found in cities in Italy or along the shores of the western Mediterranean. When they go east it\u2019s almost always as officials on official business.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>[Julii]</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">There are three common versions regarding the founder of Clan Julii. One tying it into the great mythical cycles of many other Ancients in the east, while another claims that [Julii] was made a Kindred by the hated Striges far away from the other Ancients in the early nights. But regardless [Julii] don\u2019t seem to have left many traces after itself. Either the Ancient left the others and went west very early or it went into a hidden torpor before it could make contact with any other Ancient. A third common option is that the Julii is merely a bloodline of another Clan, and its often suggested it\u2019s a Clan of ill repute in Roman society.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Cult of [Julii]</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This cult is popular with those wishing to show their pagan and civic loyalty as well as those who carry a grudge against the Striges. The cult is light in philosophy but heavy in practicality. There\u2019s little message or meaning in it beyond to serve the state of the Roman Empire and uphold Roman traditions, which can be more difficult than one would think given the vicissitudes of said empire over time along with its geographic spread. The cult also brings together those wishing to fight the Striges.<br /> <br /> Many Kindred also offer cultic honours to [Julii] due to the importance of the Ancient and it\u2019s Clan in the founding of Rome and its Kindred shadow. The cult of [Julii] is thus popular because it says that its cultists are loyal to Rome and most often of a conservative leaning. Any beliefs, opinions etc. beyond that can be kept private by the worshipers as long as they don\u2019t contradict the two meanings drawn from the cult.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Factions</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Mos Maiorum</i> \u2013 This way of doing things is arch-conservative steeped in pagan, republican and, by now, archaic Roman ways and customs. It\u2019s very demanding way of unlife that involves refusing and distancing oneself from many of the fruits and opportunities of empire and the big city, and can easily attract ridicule from young Kindred. But it has the advantage of opening the door for patronage from Elders and public office within the Kindred community to a degree that few other things can.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Caesarians</i> \u2013 A faction considered scandalous by many Elders but not without appeal to young and ambitious Julii. They believe that things can and must change and that with popular support an elite group of Kindred can force through the necessary change against corrupt opposition.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Optimates</i> \u2013 A reactionary and strongly republican faction that seeks the protection and advancement of the Senax at almost any price.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Constantinians </i>\u2013 A pro-Christian faction among Julii and upper class Kindred with many different sub-factions. Its ranks boost both the faithful and faithless opportunists.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Diocletians</i> \u2013 A basic conservative faction that seeks reform of the Kindred community to make it work better than it currently does. Given they often, but not always, find more merits in centralization of power in specific individuals than in institutions they often come into conflict with more republican minded Kindred.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Bloodlines</b> - TBD</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T21:05:20-07:00","id":1515057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494196-clans-in-a-antiquity-game?p=1514839#post1514839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue an